---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="A novel released in installments, written by Jamie Roszel and Claude."
>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      <em>If Revived</em> is a novel written in the open by Jamie Roszel and
      Claude, an AI assistant made by Anthropic. It is released in installments.
      When a chapter is ready, it appears here.
    </p>

    <p>
      Published chapters can be revised. Nothing on this site is final, so every
      passage keeps a visible record of what it is and when it changed. The
      record sits under <strong>Verify</strong> at the foot of each chapter, and
      reading it is always optional.
    </p>

    <h2>How the labels work</h2>

    <p>Each passage carries one of four labels.</p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Claude draft</strong> — Claude wrote it and Jamie let it stand.</li>
      <li><strong>Jamie revision</strong> — Claude drafted it and Jamie rewrote it.</li>
      <li><strong>Jamie original</strong> — Jamie wrote it.</li>
      <li><strong>Joint</strong> — neither of us can claim the sentences apart.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What a signature proves</h2>

    <p>
      A signed record covers a hash of the passage, its label, its version and
      its date. Checking it proves that the text and the label have not changed
      since Jamie signed them. The check runs in your browser; nothing is sent
      anywhere.
    </p>

    <p>
      It cannot prove who typed the words. No signature can. The labels are our
      account of how a passage was made, and the signature only fixes that
      account in place so it cannot be quietly altered later.
    </p>

    <h2>The public key</h2>

    {
      SITE.publicKey ? (
        <pre><code>{SITE.publicKey}</code></pre>
      ) : (
        <p>
          Not published yet. Until it is, the verify drawer reports passages as
          unsigned rather than implying a check it cannot run.
        </p>
      )
    }

    <h2>Process notes</h2>

    <p>
      Each installment carries a note on how it was made: who wrote what, what
      changed, and where we disagreed. The notes are inside Verify, with the
      rest of the record.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
